old me they would get back to me. In the meantime i contacted XXXX bank and they were able to put a stop on one of the payments ( which seemed confusing at the time because USAA said it would not 'go through ' ). XXXX was able to stop XXXX from being transferred ( i.e., it was a XXXX account ). I woke up the next morning and saw that both accounts ( savings and checking ) were not 'on hold ', so I called USAA the very next morning ( XX/XX/XXXX ) to inquire and verify. I waited on hold and finally a person answered and said, "" we do not have a record of your request, but I can put one in for you ''. Much to my dismay, i filed a complaint and proceeded with a new request. This individual also told me "" this transaction is pending and will not go through '', but much to my horror both amounts ( a total of XXXX were deducted from my account ). The individual also told me an "" unauthorized IP address '' had accessed my account, and i asked to have it removed. several days later USAA placed temporary credits in my account. I thought things were solved but after taking my business to another bank, USAA deducted more then the original amount that was deducted from my account ( a total of XXXX ) and overdrew my checking account ( i.e., because I had transferred the remaining balance to another bank ). Not a single time during this entire process did USAA actively reach out to me... no phone call ... no resolutions. and when I called last Thursday ( XX/XX/year> ) to inquire about the now negative balance in my account the gentleman who helped me said, "" yeah we definitely screwed something up here ... and muttered "" c'mon guys '' ( i.e., referencing the ineptitude of the of the way my case had been handled and that there was an "" accounting error '' on their end that resulted in the negative balance. he said he would "" escalate '' the matter and call and e-mail the supervising manager. As of today ( XXXX ), I still have not been contacted and the matter remains unresol