15797683,2025-09-08,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Old information reappears or never goes away,"To Whom It May Concern, I am writing to demand the immediate removal of an item that has been unlawfully reinserted into my credit report. Upon reviewing my recent credit report, I discovered that XXXX XXXX accounts listed under account XXXX have reappeared on XX/XX/year> after previously being deleted on XX/XX/year>. I have attached 3 screenshots, documenting the deletions of all 12 actions. I have also attached 12 screenshots, which documents your update of each account to my credit report. This action directly violates my rights under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), specifically 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ).

