15841001,2025-09-11,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Other features, terms, or problems",Other problem,"CFPB Complaint American Express Complainant : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX # XXXX XXXX XXXX, NV XXXX Company : American Express XXXX XXXX XXXX. Box XXXX XXXX XXXX, TX XXXX Issue : Arbitrary credit limit reduction and abusive account review practices, harming my credit profile and creating consumer hardship. 

Summary of Complaint I have been a loyal American Express cardholder since XXXX ( 18+ years ) with a spotless payment history. I have never been delinquent and have consistently paid down balances responsibly. Despite this, on XX/XX/XXXX, American Express suddenly reduced my credit limit from {$23000.00} to {$5300.00} ( a 77 % cut ). 
This reduction was not triggered by late payments, high utilization, or any negative behavior. In fact, the reduction occurred immediately after making a {$40.00} XXXX purchase. 
Separately, my account has been flagged multiple times within seconds of small, routine transactions ( for example, getting gas, paying for XXXX ). Each time, I received automated notices demanding XXXX  paydowns ( e.g., {$1400.00} within three days ) or risk being placed under review. 

Why This is Abusive These reviews are not fraud prevention they occur immediately after legitimate purchases. 
The forced paydowns are arbitrary, not linked to risk or delinquency. 
The drastic credit limit cut creates the false appearance of over-utilization, directly harming my credit score despite perfect repayment history. 
This practice punishes loyal, responsible customers and creates financial instability rather than promoting responsible credit use. 

Impact My available credit dropped by 77 % overnight, skewing my utilization ratio and lowering my credit score. 
I have been forced to comply with arbitrary paydown demands just to continue using my account. 
The practices have created significant stress and uncertainty around access to my own credit line, despite 18 years of loyalty and responsible use. 

Requested Resolution Immediate review and reversal of the credit limit reduction on my account. 
A clear explanation from American Express as to why my account was flagged and penalized despite no delinquency, high utilization, or risk indicators.

Regulatory review of American Express practice of slashing limits and imposing arbitrary paydown demands on long-term, responsible customers without justification. 

( Filed with American Express on XX/XX/XXXX ) I previously notified American Express in writing that these account review tactics are abusive and hostile, and that they undermine rather than support responsible credit use. I requested that my objection be placed on file with my account.",,AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY,NV,89148,,Web,2025-09-11,Closed with explanation,Yes
