15846868,2025-09-10,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am formally disputing the accuracy and legality of the collection account being reported by XXXX XXXX XXXX regarding an alleged XXXX XXXX XXXX balance. This account must be deleted immediately for the following reasons : 1. Improper Reinsertion of Deleted Account ( FCRA 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ) ) This collection account was previously deleted from my credit report after investigation. It has now been reinserted without proper notice or certification. Under FCRA 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ), if an item is deleted because it can not be verified, it can not be reinserted unless the furnisher certifies the information is accurate. The credit bureau is also required to provide me written notice within 5 business days of reinsertion. I never received such notice. This reinsertion is a direct violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act. 2. Failure to Provide Proper Validation ( FDCPA 809 ( b ) ) XXXX XXXX XXXX has not produced proper validation of the alleged debt. The only documentation provided was a self-generated balance summary that does not establish liability. They have failed to provide : A signed contract or service agreement showing I am legally responsible for this account, An itemized billing history from XXXX XXXX proving the balance, and Proof of legal assignment showing their right to collect. Without this, the debt remains unverified. 3. Furnishing Inaccurate Information ( FCRA 1681s-2, 1681i ) Despite the lack of proper validation and my dispute, XXXX continues to furnish this account to Experian, Equifax, and TransUnion. By reporting the account as active and disputed without full validation, they are furnishing incomplete and misleading information in violation of the FCRA. 4. Consumer Harm This inaccurate collection account is causing significant damage to my credit profile and financial opportunities. XXXX  unlawful actions are creating ongoing harm. Requested Action I am requesting that : The XXXX XXXX XXXX account be immediately deleted from all of my credit reports ; The credit bureaus provide me with a copy of any certification submitted by XXXX that led to the reinsertion ( if one exists ) ; XXXX XXXX XXXX cease all collection activity until proper, verifiable documentation is produced ; CFPB take action to ensure XXXX XXXX XXXX and the credit bureaus comply with FDCPA and FCRA requirements. Unless full validation is provided, this debt must be treated as unverified and permanently removed under federal law. Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NC,28216,,Web,2025-09-11,Closed with explanation,Yes
