15946746,2025-09-15,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Other features, terms, or problems",Other problem,"I am writing to file a formal complaint against Bank of America concerning a credit card account that was compromised due to what appears to be a systemic failure to adequately disclose and manage Personal Identification Numbers ( PINs ). As a result of this issue, I have been held liable for fraudulent charges despite reporting the unauthorized activity. See attached letter My credit card account, last four digit XXXX was compromised, and fraudulent charges were made using a PIN. Bank of America has denied my claim to credit back the fraudulent charges, stating that a PIN was used to authorize the transactions. My key issue is that at no point was I informed that the card came with a pre-assigned PIN, nor was I given clear instructions on how to set a new, secure one. 
