16223213,2025-09-27,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"To Whom It May Concern, This is a formal complaint under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( 15 U.S.C. 1681 ), the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act, and all other consumer protection laws regarding the continuous false and harmful late payment reporting placed on my credit reports by XXXX. The law clearly states that furnishers of information must ensure maximum possible accuracy, and consumer reporting agencies must conduct proper reinvestigations when a consumer disputes any entry. In my case, multiple accounts are being reported with late payment notations that are absolutely false and can not be verified, causing me severe damage in my financial life. 
